{
  "version": 1,
  "questionId": "q04",
  "speechText": "Recently, I worked with an AI agent workflow system called StrangeLoop. It has a Studio for configuration and an Engine for execution. Basically, the Engine runs the workflow step by step. It can call the LLM, call different tools, and make decisions along the way, and that makes the agent easier to control and debug. For example, the agent can understand the request, choose the right tool, and send it to the backend. The Engine manages the flow, and the application keeps its own data. So overall, through this project, I learned that a good agent system needs clear boundaries. The platform controls the rules and orchestration, and the application controls its own data and business actions.",
